# oracle: pair_style meam, per-triplet Cmin/Cmax (w33meamtrip_b1_lib.meam + w33meamtrip_b1.meam, zbl 0): one A-A bond screened by a B atom (the rock-salt second-neighbour geometry, screening C = 1 in the window of Cmin(1,1,2) = 0.8), plus an A-B bond, in a periodic box, run 0
# oracle: docs.lammps.org/pair_meam.html "Cmin(I,J,K) = Cmin screening parameter when I-J pair is screened by K (I<=J)"; the A-A bond is the (1,1,2) triplet
# oracle-inputs: w33meamtrip_b1_lib.meam w33meamtrip_b1.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-9
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
region          box block 0 30 0 30 0 30
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 single 10.0 10.0 10.0
create_atoms    1 single 12.6 12.6 10.0
create_atoms    2 single 12.6 10.0 10.0
mass            1 63.546
mass            2 58.69
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * w33meamtrip_b1_lib.meam A B w33meamtrip_b1.meam A B
thermo_style    custom step pe pxx pyy pzz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
